;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;
; File: system/plcmacro4.mac
; Desc: ATC Reset -- wireless MPG macro button 4
;
; The PLC maps MpgMacro4_M -> SV_SYS_MACRO = 4, which makes CNC12 load and run
; this file from \cncm\system\ while it is at the main menu. Same action as the
; VCP ATC RESET button.
;
; Why a dummy tool: CNC12 skips an M6 for the tool its status window says is
; loaded, so after a hand-moved carousel a change back to that tool is silently
; ignored -- no error, no motion -- and the PLC's hand-move interlock keeps
; refusing the spindle. Tool 200 is never the loaded tool, so this M6 always
; runs: the carousel search proves the position, the interlock clears, and
; CNC12 puts the previously loaded tool back in its bin. Follow with a real T##.
;
; Setup: tool 200 must be assigned a bin in the Tool Library, with its H and D
; offsets set to 0.
;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;

;Skip if graphing or searching
IF #4201 || #4202 THEN GOTO 1000

T200 M6         ; forces a real change: clears the skip and re-proves the bin

N1000           ; end of program
